{"id":1041705,"date":"2026-09-08T11:15:56","date_gmt":"2026-09-08T15:15:56","guid":{"rendered":"https://www.nasa.gov/?p=1041705"},"modified":"2026-09-08T11:15:58","modified_gmt":"2026-09-08T15:15:58","slug":"nasa-technique-for-manipulating-satellite-photos-now-reveals-ancient-images","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https://www.nasa.gov/technology/tech-transfer-spinoffs/nasa-technique-for-manipulating-satellite-photos-now-reveals-ancient-images/","title":{"rendered":"NASA Technique for Manipulating Satellite Photos Now Reveals Ancient Images  "},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"\" class=\"padding-top-5 padding-bottom-3 width-full maxw-full hds-module hds-module-full alignfull wp-block-nasa-blocks-article-intro\"><div class=\"width-full maxw-full article-header\"><div class=\"margin-bottom-2 width-full maxw-full\"><p class=\"label carbon-60 margin-0 margin-bottom-3 padding-0\">3 min read</p><h1 class=\"display-48 margin-bottom-2\">NASA Technique for Manipulating Satellite Photos Now Reveals Ancient Images  </h1></div></div></div>\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-media hds-module wp-block-image\"><div class=\"margin-left-auto margin-right-auto nasa-block-align-inline\"><div class=\"hds-media-wrapper margin-left-auto margin-right-auto\"><figure class=\"hds-media-inner hds-cover-wrapper hds-media-ratio-none \"><a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1575\" height=\"2048\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?w=1575\" class=\"attachment-2048x2048 size-2048x2048\" alt=\"A man stands in front of a rock with art on it, the colors are intense and exaggerated revealing an intricate design in the rock&#039;s surface.\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 50%; object-position: 50% 50%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg 1972w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=231,300 231w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=768,999 768w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=788,1024 788w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=1181,1536 1181w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=1575,2048 1575w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=308,400 308w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=461,600 461w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=692,900 692w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=923,1200 923w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-4b.jpeg?resize=1538,2000 1538w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1575px) 100vw, 1575px\" /></a></figure><figcaption class=\"hds-caption padding-y-2\"><div class=\"hds-caption-text p-sm margin-0\">Jon Harman poses in front of an example of the Rancho Bernardo style of Native American artwork that’s barely visible until Dstretch is applied. </div><div class=\"hds-credits\">Credit: Jon Harman </div></figcaption></div></div></div>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">High in&nbsp;the central tower in the ancient Cambodian temple&nbsp;of&nbsp;Angkor Wat, paintings depict horseback riders and a traditional musical ensemble.&nbsp;Thousands of visitors pass these images&nbsp;daily&nbsp;without noticing, because&nbsp;they’re&nbsp;faded to the point of invisibility.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They were discovered&nbsp;between 2010 and 2012, along with about 200 other paintings throughout the complex, by an&nbsp;archaeologist using a method conceived at NASA’s Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Southern California.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The technique, known as decorrelation stretch, heightens contrasts in digital imagery, making&nbsp;features easier to spot.&nbsp;It&nbsp;is&nbsp;especially&nbsp;popular&nbsp;for studying ancient rock art,&nbsp;partly&nbsp;due to the chance intersection of one man’s hobby with his professional background.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Around 2005,&nbsp;rock art enthusiast Jon Harman&nbsp;saw&nbsp;NASA&nbsp;images depicting the Martian surface with and without the application of decorrelation stretch. Seeing how much detail the technique revealed,&nbsp;Harman, now retired in Pacifica, California,&nbsp;understood the implication for studying ancient, faded images.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He also worked&nbsp;in medical imaging. “I Googled it and found a NASA paper that explained how to do the algorithm,” he said. “I knew from my medical imaging experience that I could do it, so I did.”&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The paper was written in 1996 by Ronald Alley, a JPL employee developing&nbsp;applications&nbsp;for the Advanced Spaceborne Thermal Emission and Reflection Radiometer (ASTER), a Japanese&nbsp;imaging&nbsp;instrument on NASA’s Terra satellite.&nbsp;One of&nbsp;Alley’s former supervisors&nbsp;at JPL&nbsp;had&nbsp;coinvented decorrelation stretch, and Alley had recognized its potential for gleaning information from ASTER imagery.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Harman made his plug-in for use with ImageJ,&nbsp;an open-source program developed by the National Institutes of Health.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-media hds-module aligncenter wp-block-nasa-blocks-image-before-after\">\n\t<div class=\"NasaBlocksImageBeforeAfterBlock grid-container grid-row grid-container-block bg-spacesuit-white padding-x-0 padding-y-6 margin-x-auto nasa-block-align-center\">\n\t\t<div class=\"padding-x-0 grid-col-12\">\n\n\t\t\t<!-- curtain view -->\n\t\t\t<div class=\"img-comparison-slider-parent comparison-view-active\">\n\t\t\t\t<img-comparison-slider>\n\t\t\t\t\t<img decoding=\"async\" slot=\"first\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg\" alt=\"\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<img decoding=\"async\" slot=\"second\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg\" alt=\"\">\n\t\t\t\t</img-comparison-slider>\n\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"curtain-view-label-wrapper curtain-view-before\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"curtain-view-label\">before</span>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"curtain-view-label-wrapper curtain-view-after\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"curtain-view-label\">after</span>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t<!-- toggle view -->\n\t\t\t<div class=\"toggle-comparison-parent\">\n\t\t\t\t<!-- if image_1 is active the show image_1 -->\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"hds-media-wrapper margin-left-auto margin-right-auto\"><figure class=\"hds-media-inner hds-cover-wrapper hds-media-ratio-cover toggle-view-image toggle-view-before-image toggle-view-active\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"768\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?w=768\" class=\"attachment-medium_large size-medium_large\" alt=\"A wall with a series of faded humanoid figures painted on it.\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 33%; object-position: 50% 33%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg 2592w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=200,300 200w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=768,1152 768w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=683,1024 683w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=1024,1536 1024w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=1365,2048 1365w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=267,400 267w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=400,600 400w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=600,900 600w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=800,1200 800w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=1333,2000 1333w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /></figure></div>\n\t\t\t\t<!-- if image_2 is active the show image_2 -->\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"hds-media-wrapper margin-left-auto margin-right-auto\"><figure class=\"hds-media-inner hds-cover-wrapper hds-media-ratio-cover toggle-view-image toggle-view-after-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"768\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?w=768\" class=\"attachment-medium_large size-medium_large\" alt=\"A new yellow figure emerges from behind the other after the dstretch algorithm is applied\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 49% 34%; object-position: 49% 34%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg 2592w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=200,300 200w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=768,1152 768w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=683,1024 683w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=1024,1536 1024w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=1365,2048 1365w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=267,400 267w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=400,600 400w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=600,900 600w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=800,1200 800w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=1333,2000 1333w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /></figure></div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"toggle-button-container padding-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<button class=\"toggle-view-before-button toggle-comparison-view-active margin-right-1px\"><span class=\"toggle-view-before-label\">before</span></button><button class=\"toggle-view-after-button margin-left-1px\"><span class=\"toggle-view-after-label\">after</span></button>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t<!-- 2-up view -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"two-up-view position-relative bg-carbon-10\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col flex-3 padding-top-4 padding-bottom-4\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"hds-media-wrapper margin-left-auto margin-right-auto\"><figure class=\"hds-media-inner hds-cover-wrapper hds-media-ratio-cover \"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"768\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?w=768\" class=\"attachment-medium_large size-medium_large\" alt=\"A wall with a series of faded humanoid figures painted on it.\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 33%; object-position: 50% 33%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg 2592w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=200,300 200w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=768,1152 768w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=683,1024 683w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=1024,1536 1024w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=1365,2048 1365w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=267,400 267w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=400,600 400w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=600,900 600w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=800,1200 800w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3a.jpeg?resize=1333,2000 1333w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /></figure></div>\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"bg-spacesuit-white width-2px\"></div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col flex-3 padding-top-4 padding-bottom-4\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"hds-media-wrapper margin-left-auto margin-right-auto\"><figure class=\"hds-media-inner hds-cover-wrapper hds-media-ratio-cover \"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"768\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?w=768\" class=\"attachment-medium_large size-medium_large\" alt=\"A new yellow figure emerges from behind the other after the dstretch algorithm is applied\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 49% 34%; object-position: 49% 34%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg 2592w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=200,300 200w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=768,1152 768w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=683,1024 683w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=1024,1536 1024w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=1365,2048 1365w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=267,400 267w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=400,600 400w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=600,900 600w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=800,1200 800w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/dstretch-3b.jpeg?resize=1333,2000 1333w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\" /></figure></div>\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"curtain-view-label-wrapper curtain-view-before\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"curtain-view-label\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tbefore\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"curtain-view-label-wrapper curtain-view-after\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class=\"curtain-view-label\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tafter\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t<!-- Under image content -->\n\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row flex-row title-row padding-x-2 desktop:padding-x-0 padding-top-2\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 tablet:grid-col-6\">\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p class=\"before-after-heading margin-bottom-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tBefore and After\t\t\t\t\t</p>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"before-after-title margin-top-0 margin-bottom-1\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\tDstretch applied to Cave of San Borjitas in Baja California, Mexico\t\t\t\t\t</h2>\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 tablet:grid-col-6 button-row margin-bottom-3 tablet:margin-bottom-0\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<!-- Update onClick handlers -->\n\t\t\t\t\t<button\n\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Curtain view\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"comparison-view curtain-view-button comparison-view-active padding-bottom-1 margin-left-1\"\n\t\t\t\t\t>Curtain</button><button\n\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Toggle view\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"comparison-view toggle-view-button padding-bottom-1 margin-left-1\"\n\t\t\t\t\t>Toggle</button><button\n\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Two-Up view\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"comparison-view two-up-view-button padding-bottom-1 margin-left-1\"\n\t\t\t\t\t>2-Up</button>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t<!-- Image detail area -->\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"image-details-panel padding-x-0\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"before-after-details-divider padding-y-2\">\n\t\t\t\t<!-- OnClick handleImageDetailsClick --><button class=\"image-details-toggle-button\"><span>Image Details</span><!-- style - if showImageDetails, then transform rotate(180deg), else none --><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 15\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"7.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke=\"#58585B\" /><path fill-rule=\"evenodd\" clip-rule=\"evenodd\" d=\"M7.0002 8.23854L9.26318 5.95996L9.80019 6.50067L7.0002 9.31996L4.2002 6.50067L4.73721 5.95996L7.0002 8.23854Z\" fill=\"#58585B\" /></svg></button>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t<!-- if showImageDetails, then display -->\n\t\t\t<div id=\"image-details\" class=\" padding-x-0\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-row\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"grid-col flex-2\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"image-details-wrapper\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAs Jon Harman was developing the Dstretch plug-in, he applied it to this image from the Cave of San Borjitas in Baja California, Mexico. When the yellow figure appeared in the middle of the picture, he knew he had something useful. Credit: Jon Harman \t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<!-- File List -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n\n\t</div>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He&nbsp;said he&nbsp;fulfills&nbsp;about 200 requests&nbsp;for&nbsp;Dstretch&nbsp;per year. Around 2010, he&nbsp;also&nbsp;created smartphone apps that use a shortcut to mimic decorrelation stretch. The apps have been downloaded thousands of times, and papers have been published describing Dstretch’s usefulness in archaeology.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It has been used to spot and clarify imagery at ancient sites under a cliff in Norway, in an Egyptian tomb, at a park in Canada, and&nbsp;in&nbsp;many&nbsp;other&nbsp;locations.&nbsp;It has also helped archaeologists find buried remains of ancient Greek buildings and examine tattoos on mummified human&nbsp;remains, among its non-rock-art applications.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Harman said he was not surprised Dstretch found wide use in the rock art community. “But&nbsp;I’ve&nbsp;been surprised by a lot of the different applications people have found. So&nbsp;that’s&nbsp;been cool.”&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"nasa-gb-align-center nasa-button-link padding-y-1 padding-x-0 hds-module aligncenter wp-block-nasa-blocks-related-link\">\n\t<a href=\"https://spinoff.nasa.gov/Manipulating_Satellite_Photos_Now_Reveals_Ancient_Images\" target=\"_self\" class=\"button-primary button-primary-md link-external-true\" aria-label=\"Read more about Read More\" rel=\"noopener\">\n\t\t<span class=\"line-height-alt-1\">Read More</span>\n\t\t<svg viewBox=\"0 0 32 32\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><circle class=\"button-primary-circle\" cx=\"16\" cy=\"16\" r=\"16\"></circle><path d=\"M8 16.956h12.604l-3.844 4.106 1.252 1.338L24 16l-5.988-6.4-1.252 1.338 3.844 4.106H8v1.912z\" class=\"color-spacesuit-white\"></path></svg>\n\t</a>\n\n\t</div>\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"nasa-gb-align-full width-full maxw-full padding-x-3 padding-y-0 nasa_template_article_a hds-module hds-module-full alignfull wp-block-nasa-blocks-credits-and-details\">\n<section class=\"padding-x-0 padding-top-5 padding-bottom-2 desktop:padding-top-7 desktop:padding-bottom-9\">\n\t<div class=\"grid-row grid-container maxw-widescreen padding-0\">\n\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-2 padding-right-4 margin-bottom-5 desktop:margin-bottom-0\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"padding-top-3 border-top-1px border-color-carbon-black\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"margin-bottom-2\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"heading-14\">Share</h2>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"padding-bottom-2\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<ul class=\"social-icons social-icons-round\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"social-icon social-icon-x\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://x.com/intent/tweet?via=NASA&#038;text=NASA%C2%A0Technique%20for%20Manipulating%20Satellite%20Photos%20Now%20Reveals%20Ancient%20Images%C2%A0%C2%A0&#038;url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nasa.gov